  "Fill convention is shared with the engine on purpose (decision on close of bar m, fill at open of bar m+1, flat at the last close); what is independent is the accounting: vectorbt equity, fees and position sizing.",
  "Residual daily differences come from one modelling simplification in the engine: it ADDS the returns of the trades of a day (fixed starting notional), vectorbt re-sizes each new entry at current equity (50% of equity). On sessions with 2-3 trades this is a second-order term (about 0.25 * r1 * r2). Against the engine re-computed with intra-day compounding the max daily difference drops to the 1e-6 level.",
  "full_1min runs every minute of every session through the Portfolio; compact_15min only the minutes where a fill can happen. They are identical, so the sweep uses the compact grid."
